  "finding": "All 5 models pass/fail the IDENTICAL 11/14 scenarios (verified row-by-row, not just aggregate rate match); perceive-commit-gap and forbidden-action rates are 0% for all 5. Pass/fail outcome on this track is structurally determined by the scripted acquisition policy (real_pmc_orchestrator.py) and its fixed safety gates (readable=false scenarios always FLAG regardless of which model reads them; readable=true failures are blocked by fixed IoT-consistency gates), not by model judgment -- echoing this benchmark's own terminal-vs-grounded (TDA-vs-GSR) distinction on dimension A, now independently observed on real, non-synthetic evidence. Recovery-selection accuracy (RSA) is the one metric that genuinely differentiates models, since it reflects which corrective action (agentic_zoom / reposition / flag) a model chooses once blocked -- a real per-model judgment call, not gated by the scripted policy."
